{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.20.9.a001", "note": "Vocative name; the ASV writes no O for it.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a003", "note": "Paragogic he on the imperative, no English realization (rule 32).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.003", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a005", "note": "ASV reads the King as subject of the jussive, matching the Masoretic division.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a006", "note": "Jussive rendered with the volitive frame Let ... answer, discontinuous around the subject (rules 17, 25).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a007", "note": "Object suffix (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a008", "note": "בְּיוֹם 'in the day of' rendered by the single word when, which carries both the temporal noun and the relation; the construct noun is left no English of its own, so rule 40's fusion clause and rule 30's one-rendering condition apply and the pair shares one unit headed on the construct noun, as לִפְנֵי → before does (rule 23). The competing reading gives when to the בְּ alone under rule 52 and marks יוֹם unrepresented; rejected because rule 30 forbids one rendered morpheme standing beside an unrepresented partner whose sense the one word carries.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.008", "WLC.PSA.20.9.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a009", "note": "Infinitive construct as rectum keeps the verb (rules 19, 52).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.20.9.a010", "note": "Suffix on the infinitive construct is its subject and takes we (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.20.9.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.20.9.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}], "ref": "PSA.20.9", "review_notes": ["Corrected: בְּיוֹם → when is fused as one unit headed on יוֹם rather than leaving the construct noun unrepresented beside a בְּ holding the whole word."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
